Deterministic fuzz smoke (2026-10-13 07:33:39 UTC):
- Added fixture-seeded, fixed-budget mutation coverage for Remoting frames/JSON and private headers/ext fields, message records/properties, and bounded Zlib/LZ4/Zstd decompression. The same harness is part of ordinary Remoting tests and has an isolated `fuzz_smoke` example. Unknown 32-bit JSON and representable private-header request codes round-trip without registry filtering.
- First run exposed the private-header signed 16-bit request-code encoding boundary when 987654 was selected for the binary codec. Kept the large unknown-code probe on JSON and added a private-header unknown code within its wire range; no implementation behavior was changed.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --test fuzz_regressions --locked`; `cargo run -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --example fuzz_smoke --locked` (103 Remoting seeds, 10 message seeds, 1,808 mutations, 144 successful frame decodes, 95 successful message decodes); strict Remoting all-target/all-feature Clippy; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`.
- The bounded decoder limits cap frame/record input at 64 KiB and decompressed bodies at 4 KiB.


Deterministic race/leak smoke (2026-10-13 07:33:48 UTC):
- Added `tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh` and its coverage map. The fail-closed runner requires each filter to execute at least one passing test and repeats 16 named cases three times. It covers remoting pending/opaque/deadline/cancel/shutdown, socket publication, GO_AWAY reconnect, concurrent runtime creation, request/reply terminal ownership/admission, consumer assignment churn and offset/lock generation fencing.
- PASS: `bash tests/stress/run-offline-smoke.sh` (all 48 executions passed; each test confirmed at least one matching case).
- All runs use locked local scripted or paused-time tests. No Docker or Broker was started.
